  "description": "Rear garden: Felling to ground level of T1 (Hornbeam) by way of controlled dismantle using climbing and controlled lowering techniques downto ground level. Reasons for felling are: (i) T1 is too big and has outgrown its location, (ii) it causes excessive shade in the garden which hasmeant no grass has ever been able to grow, (iii) it blocks light to the house, predominantly the kitchen where we will be spending a significantamount of time and thus be particularly impacted by this. We would look to replace T2 with a 2m acer or a 1.5m cornus kousa.",
